{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1344875-dark-eras-fan-constantinople-\u2013-early-medieval-istanbul-turkey-\u2013-700-\u2013-1000-ad","id":1344875,"title":"[Dark Eras fan] Constantinople \u2013 Early Medieval Istanbul, Turkey \u2013 700 \u2013 1000 AD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-31T03:18:31-07:00","id":1344875,"title":"[Dark Eras fan] Constantinople \u2013 Early Medieval Istanbul, Turkey \u2013 700 \u2013 1000 AD","content":"Split mini-setting from my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire\">Byzantine Empire fan Dark Era</a>, after <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1271801-dark-eras-fan-kuaru-%E2%80%93-early-medieval-kiev-ukraine-%E2%80%93-circa-700-%E2%80%93-988-ad\">Medieval Kiev</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1320068-dark-eras-fan-odessos%E2%80%93-early-medieval-odessa-ukraine-%E2%80%93-circa-500-%E2%80%93-1055-ad\">Medieval Odessa</a>. I split topic from main Byzantine Empire topic, as local setting, it\u2019s easier to digest than going through six pages of general topic. This setting is centered on first contacts of Byzantium with Vikings, being part of official <b><i>Wolf &amp; Raven</i> </b>( from <b>Dark Eras </b>1 book ) background. Years 700 \u2013 1000 AD are pointed as start of Vikings journeys in Europe and their visitations in Constantinople - till year 988 AD, when Emperor <i>Basil II</i> forms so called Varangian Guard, that becomes elite unit in Byzantine army. But let\u2019s come to short summary for those not knowing Byzantine Era it itself \u2013 full information\u2019s are to be read in Byzantine Empire Dark Era topic itself.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Constantinople &amp; Byzantine Empire</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Constantinople</b> \u2013 now known as Istanbul in Turkey \u2013 is ancient city that was second capitol of Roman Empire. When ancient Empire on West had very difficult managed it\u2019s huge lands in early 300s AD, Emperor <i>Constantine the Great</i> rebuild older Greek city of <i>Byzantium</i> as new capitol in 324 AD \u2013 and renamed it on his name, as <i>Constantinople</i> in year 330 AD. After that, line of successors of Emperors fought if Rome or Constantinople should be real capitol of Roman Empire. Finally, in in 395 AD <i>Theodosius I </i>bequeathed the imperial office jointly to his sons: <i>Arcadius</i> in the East and <i>Honorius</i> in the West, dividing Imperial administration, de facto splitting Roman Empire in to two. When Rome on West fell to barbarians, Constantinopole on East prospered. Citizens of Eastern Empire till it\u2019s fell to Turks in 1453 AD used calling of &quot;<i>Rh\u014dmais</i>&quot; (Greek: \u1fec\u03c9\u03bc\u03b1\u0390\u03c2 for \u2018Romans\u2019 ) for themselves \u2013 even then all around called them popularly \u2018Greeks\u2019. Name <i>Byzantium </i>was still used for this new capitol city on common terms, even if not Empire itself.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Eastern Orthodox Church</b></span><br /> <br /> On the start of 1<sup>st</sup> millennium, there was One Church of Christians. There where heresies, but on general, Church was that of from Rome. When on 3<sup>rd</sup> century onward Rome slowly christened, Byzantine Empire from it\u2019s start was \u2018first Christian Empire\u2019, as it was often called. <i>Constantine the Great </i>was great supporter of Christianity \u2013 and by this, Catholic Church \u2013 making it de facto official religion of Empire in 325 on equal footings with pagan worship, on First Council of Nicaea. From then on, both Rome and Byzantium become great lights from what Christian faith spread on the world \u2013 with Constantinople literally being built on it.<br /> <br /> But then Western Roman Empire fell. In the times of this setting \u2013 years circa 700 \u2013 1000 AD \u2013 there are already big changes in Church of Constantinopole. In 629 AD, Greek became, instead of Latin, official language of Byzantium \u2013 also in liturgy. Eastern Church traditions become more and more different from this of Rome \u2013 creating the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantine_Rite\" target=\"_blank\">Byzantine Rite</a>. Not without influence on situation were <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1168431#post1168431\">Iconclasm Wars</a> in 8<sup>th</sup> and 9<sup>th</sup> century inside Byzantium. All this slowly leads to Eastern Church paying only lip service to Pope in Rome in setting\u2019s times \u2013 even if officially, Constantinopole is still part of Roman Church. It all finally ends in 1054 AD, in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East%E2%80%93West_Schism\" target=\"_blank\">Great Schism</a>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Varangians \u2013 Vikings on Middle East</b></span><br /> <br /> On the end of 8<sup>th</sup> century, Vikings \u2013 brave pirates and traders from Scandinavia \u2013 are invading Europe. They also come to Constantinople. Most came from nowadays Sweden, by route of Kievan Rus, Black Sea \u2013 and then to capitol of Empire. ( By so called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trade_route_from_the_Varangians_to_the_Greeks\" target=\"_blank\">route from the Varangians to the Greeks</a> ).<br /> <br /> Varangians come both as invaders \u2013 but also bodyguards and traders to be for rent. First official documents mention in 839 AD Rus ( Slavic nativeted Vikings in Ukraine ) representatives arrived at the Frankish court as part of a Byzantine diplomatic mission. Archaeological evidence suggests Rus trading activities along the Volga trade route as early as the end of the 8th century, so it\u2019s possible they could be in Constantinople even before that date. From year 988 AD Norse are part of constant, elite formation of <i>Varangian Guard</i>, begin bodyguards to Emperor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-31-2019, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T03:20:42-07:00","id":1344879,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Monsters Society \u2013 Sworn</b></span><br /> <br /> Idea for my fan setting is that in cosmopolitan Byzantium of that time, monster works in Sworn cross-factions, after canonical Plague of Justinian being danger to the both mortals and supernatural beings. There maybe not \u2018Parliament of Night\u2019 of original Rome \u2013 in form of Senex \u2013 but many inhuman factions create lose cliques that rise to prominence with each next comings of Contagion in Byzantium region \u2013 and fight against one another in between those. Each group need for at least 1-2 leaders in Constantinopole, good are other members of those. If you have ideas on those \u2013 feel free to propose or write yours. We can also do 2E fan updates for canonical characters, like those in Byzantine setting from <b>Fall of Camarilla</b> book.<br /> <br /> Without further ado\u2026<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sworn of Justinian</b></span><br /> <br /> In 6<sup>th</sup> century after Christ, first Plague hit Byzantium. It started vicious cycle of sickness and death that took tall of almost one third of Eastern Roman Empire, across next three centuries. And it bring Sworn to fight it.<br /> <br /> At the rules of Emperor Justinian I, in one year, from 541 to 542 \u2013 pandemic of Plague killed 40% of population of Constantinople. What mortals did not known, was that (later called ) Black Death had also supernatural dimension. Some of those that died from illness, had return to life. And then died again. And return to life. And died again. Being locked in this miserable cycle, they still spread the disease, adding next to damned army of living dead. Numbers were not enough to call the open battlefield \u2013 but those of night-dwellers races known they need to respond or the secret of their existence will be broken. They need to eradicate this sickness.<br /> <br /> Lancea Sanctum ruling Constantinople - joined by newly formed Legions of Damned from previous Legio Mortuum regiments - is trying to solve epidemic on it\u2019s own. Sanctified need to do this, because from over century Camarilla de facto is no more \u2013 even when few in Kindred society still use it\u2019s name. Finally, sickness pass from Rome of East \u2013 was it workings of vampires, God Machine or mages \u2013 is to this day hotly debated. Most would agree it was will of God ( or gods ).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Convention and Splitting</b></span><br /> <br /> Sensing that Death can return to Empire, Aelia Scaevola, a Nosferatu researcher with few others children of the night started secret convention of scholars to seek ways to stop the next outbreak. They found under city ancient tomb that foretold great disaster. And those researchers spill over Empire, to look clues for the secret.<br /> <br /> It was Aelia who remembered 25 years later that sigil found in tomb to come from times of Cyrus in Achaemenid Empire, twelve hundred years earlier. Mage from Cyrus times, Vishtapa, found first signs of Contagion in their country. As Scaevola was from Lance and Spear, she was versed in Scriptures \u2013 and instantly remembered the prophecy of Jeremiah about the Fall of Babylon. She spread the idea with her colleagues and soon joined by other of monsters believing that Plague of Justinian was God\u2019s Judgment \u2013 and only faith, zeal and morality can save night-dwellers and mortals from next outbreak. They quickly infiltrated the Church and lesser cults in Empire \u2013 or rather were there from beginning - looking over ways to please the God ( and gods ). <i>Jeremiad</i> Sworn were created.<br /> <br /> But not every researcher from convention of the tomb agreed with Aelia. Some mystics were looking inside their own mind and souls for answers. Mages and beasts that seen discovery and sigil from tomb looked a lot like Omphalos Stone inside Astral Space they visit routinely on their journeys. They focused on understanding it\u2019s meaning and how dreams can help cure the Plague. Both rivalry Orders of Awakened, Panscryptia and Keepers of the World, agreed ( for the first time ) on importance of Sacred Stone. Joined by Despoina, the Mother of Bones, chthonian vampires priestess of Echidna from Athens, adversary of Scaevola, they started their own group. <i>Omphalos</i> Sworn were created.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Athanatoi</b></span><br /> <br /> Those two Sworn groups were unchallenged by few decades, where last remnants of Camarilla were trying to rise up in Night Society, however without success. Curse of Hasdrubal hanged on everything that originated from Rome itself. Ayzebel, sister-in-law to Carthages general that Curse take it\u2019s name \u2013 the same women that became creator of those that in modern night we call Cryptocracy \u2013 was Embraced and joined Camarilla in Eternal City and strive to end Contagion in Italy with like-minded. She felt with the Senex itself, but her disciple went to Byzantium with Constantine The Great. Chaos in the city did not let them took their roots. Until Senex was no more. Kindred needed new system of ruling \u2013 mortals in Empire gave them.<br /> <br /> Themata province system was created in the mid-7th century in the aftermath of the Slavic invasion of the Balkans and Muslim conquests of parts of Byzantine territory. It overturned older Roman system the strict division of civil and military offices. With new ruling system forming on their eyes, disciples of Ayzebel went for power and to control Plague, for the good of Empire. New group stated they want to stable society and give victories with Contagion for the Byzantium. They become nation sensitive leaders monsters. At the dawn of year 700s. they called themselves <i>Athanatoi</i>, Immortals. New Sworn were created in Byzantium.<br /> <br /> 10<sup>th</sup> century, mortals elite military under this conspiracy would call themselves the same.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sworn and False of Byzantine Empire</b></span><br /> In brackets are names for modern counterparts of those groups. Historical factions use mechanics the same as their nowdays decendents.<br /> <br /> <b>Sworn of this Era:</b><ul><li><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-jeremiad-contagion-chronicle/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Jeremiad</b></a> - <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Religious and morality-centred monsters. Connected to mortal ( future ) Orthodox Church. After 6th century and it\u2019s Plague of Justinian \u2013 most influential Sworn faction. <b>Typical members:</b> Lancea et Sanctum, beasts, hunters, mummies and Prometheans. Joins them Integrators, Hunters in Darkness and Lucifuge.</div></div> </div> </div></li> <li><b><i>Athanatoi </i></b>(<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-cryptocracy-contagion-chronicle/\" target=\"_blank\">Cryptocracy</a>) \u2013 <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Monsters sustaining government and rules in Empire. They are remnants from original Camarilla of Rome \u2013 and future part of Invictus. Connected mostly to Themata province system. <b>Typical members:</b> Athanatoi Convenat ( rests of Camarilla, future Invictus ), beasts, demons, mages and vampires. Join to them Adamantine Arrow, Blood Talons, Iron Masters, Storm Lords, Winter, Spring &amp; Summer Courts, Maa-Kep, and Undertakers from Sin-Eaters. </div></div> </div> </div></li> <li><b><i>Omphalos</i></b> (Rosetta Society) \u2013 <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Researches of sacred and secret, they name comes both title for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omphalos\" target=\"_blank\">mythological stone letting to communicate directly with gods</a> \u2013 and Astral Space barrier that many mages and beasts find in their journeys. <b>Typical members: </b>mages from Keepers of the Word and Pancryptiates Orders ( in 12<sup>th</sup> century they merge into modern Mysterium, but in this Dark Eras they compete inside Sworn ), beasts, demons, changelings, hunters and werewolves. Joins too them Bone Shadows, Circle of the Crone, Mekhet vampires, Sesha-Hebsu, Mourners from Sin-Eaters and Tammuz. </div></div> </div> </div></li> </ul><b>False of this Era:</b><br /> <br /> \u00b7<b><i>Horde</i> </b>(Naglfar\u2019s Army) \u2013 <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Literal \u2018barbarians at the gates\u2019 \u2013 and on the inside. Over centuries, Easter Roman Empire had many enemies \u2013 Huns, Khazars, Arabs, Vikings, Ottamans and many, many others. Each of this groups was coming with next war that could \u2018end the world\u2019. What was joining them was secret support of night-dwellers, wanting to tear down Empire, once and for all. However Horde was not only on the outside \u2013 but was infiltrating Night Society in the inside. From the times of Ancient Rome, at least handful of monsters were doing their own \u2018Saturnalia\u2019, preparing for the end of world. With enemies on the outside and inside \u2013 Byzantine Empire finally was no more. In 900\u2019s Horde dogma mixed with Vikings legends of Ragnarok \u2013 and modern Naglfar\u2019s Army was created from there.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T08:20:58-07:00","id":1344946,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Monsters Society, p. 2 \u2013 Members of Sworn</b></span><br /> <br /> Here is list of basic NPCs concepts filling Sworn numbers in Constantinople. I will edit later this post with simple sum-ups and links to posts with proper members write-ups. I put design comments in \u2018//\u2019 marks.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Jeremiad</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Iovinus \u2013 Archbishop of Constantinople ( called Patriarch )</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Clan</b>: Daeva<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Ag\u00eda Lans ( gr. Lancea Sanctum )<br /> <br /> Iovinus is reformator. After centuries of separate veneration from mortals, Lancea et Sanctum need to start following belief much more like mortals \u2013 or the questions will rise too much in daylight society. Even if he is not lifting Third Tradition of Timothy that banned worship with mortals - Iovinus is putting elements of Byzantine Rite to his black masses in Cisterns under Hagia Sophia, in Byzantium city. He is forcing old Roman natured Elders to speak in Greek, like Romanoi around them. He worries that next Plague can hit capitol because vampires stands too much from their kin and God will show his wrath on Constantinopole for breaking Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <b>Uratha Pack - <i>Kun\u0113g\u00f3skula tou Theo\u00fa </i>( Hounds of God )</b><br /> <br /> Pack of Hunters in Darkness werewolves, guarding area around and under Hagia Sophia, with crossing rights granted for Lancea Sanctum vampires, inside Jeremiad Sworn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Athanatoi</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Vetranis</b> <b>\u2013 Dominus Noctis Imperator</b><br /> <br /> <b>Clan</b>: Julii<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> <br /> <b>Jaromir \u2013 Slavic Strategos</b><br /> <br /> <b>Clan</b>: Gangrel<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> / Strategos are \u2018generals of Emperor in terrain\u2019. Jaromir is previous Slavic commander of military, now in the Byzantine army. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> /<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Omphalos</b></span><br /> <b><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Uratha Pack - Timov\u00edtes ton Cham\u00e9non Al\u00edtheias ( Cenobites of Lost Truths )</span></b></b><br /> <br /> Pack of Bone Shadows werewolves, guarding Imperial Library of Constantinople, with help from various mages of Keepers of the Word Order.<br /> <br /> <b>Tr\u00f3gon ton Nekr\u00f3n ( Eater of Dead )</b><br /> <br /> <b>Auspice</b>: Ithaeur<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Bone Shadows<br /> Trogon is blind monk working in Imperial Library. He is also Alpha of Timovites, leading his wolf brothers and sisters in duty of making sure Library has all the books in papyrus and parchment rest in peace.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Horde</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Hafgrim \u2013 Viking General</b><br /> <br /> <b>Clan</b>: Gangrel<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> ???<br /> Hafgrim is one of generals that lead next siege of Constantinople. He is also brutish vampire, surviving in the sun when need to lead his armies. Embraced against his will, he miss the daylight. He seeks Contagion as way for resurrecting himself in to sun light, once and for all.<br /> <br /> / Do not know what Covenants were in Viking vampires society, if any. Maybe Belial Brood? But it\u2019s not sure in 2E <b>VtR</b>, I think? /","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-01-2019, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T23:32:09-07:00","id":1345398,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Monsters Society, p. 3 \u2013 Vampires Government \u2013 Night Emperor, Patriarch and Prisci Council</b></span><br /> <br /> Kindred society of Constantinople is governed like that of mortal \u2013 just much more stable. When in living Empire, ruler can be change for complete stranger in one, two decades \u2013 undead are much more certain in their choices. Mostly because they are virtually immortal. If he is clever in his politics, new <i>Dominus Noctis Imperator</i> ( Great Night Imperator ) is chosen once in few centuries when previous one is going to Torpor, from Prisci Council \u2013 leaders of Clans in city, and by this, in Empire. New Imperator is appointing now <i>Stratoegoi</i> ( sing. <i>Strategos </i>) \u2013 generals in the field, to look over his matters for him in Empire, under sacred Oaths to him. All other them are watched if they making will of God by the<i> Patriarch of the Damned</i>, <i>Vicar of Longinus</i>, <i>Archbishop of Constantinople. </i>Sanctified Patriarch and Imperator rule almost as co-princes, with Imperator taking matters of world and Patriarch those of souls.<br /> <br /> Within city, Kindred are divided into <i>thema</i>, administrative groups (usually divided by lineage) with specific responsibilities to the Kindred government who gained specific rights in return, usually in regard to where they might haven and feed. The <i>Mystikoi</i>, a line of Gangrel monks, serve as scribes and historians, for example, and are given the right to feed from the city\u2019s monastic population.<br /> <br /> Nowadays rules of Imperator and Prisci Council ( 700-1000 AD ) is result of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plague_of_Justinian\" target=\"_blank\">Justinian Plague</a> of 541 ( with it\u2019s repeated resurgences till 750 AD ) \u2013 called centuries later Black Death. With as high as 40% mortality rate in Empire, it took many of humans supplies and networks of older Roman Elders \u2013 leading to their downfall or even Final Death. With humans dying en masse and normal dead returning to \u2018life\u2019 \u2013 Kindred needed change of rules. With old Patriarch lost in tumult and Prisci Council finally dead, vampires looked for new leaders. It came with <i>Ventranis</i> \u2013 previous barbarians hordes leader from West that became general in Days Emperor armies. He with few others Ancillae helped new appointed Patriarch Ivonius enforced order in Plague stricken Constantinopole. Following traditions of living Eastern Roman Empire, he was anointed Dominus Noctis Imperator by Ivonius \u2013 and start it\u2019s rules as King ( or rather, Emperor ) of Night in Reigning City. He appointed his helpers as Prisci that now advise him in ranks of Athanatoi. Researchers in Imperial Library whispers that they found legend about Imperator\u2019s name giver \u2013 Ven \u2013 being connected to stories of Troy and creation of Julii Clan of old\u2026<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Dominus Noctis Imperator \u2013 Ventranis</b></span><br /> <b>Clan: \u2018Ven\u2019 ( future Ventrue )</b><br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>482 CE ( same as birth of Emperor Justinian )<br /> <br /> Centuries ago, Ventranis was commander of one of next barbarian armies that lead siege on Constantinople. What was not known \u2013 he already was vampire of ancient noble and leaders Clan spread inside \u2018uncivilised\u2019 lands. Some rumours said he is related to Julii, somehow. His strategic mind and acumen lead him to become Day Emperors Justinian general, helping, in the end, to defend Byzantium. He hid his vampiric condition as \u2018foreign customs of his people\u2019 \u2013 and led small politics in Empire. Then came the Plague and everything changed. Without Prisci Council and with old Patriarch missing, there was chaos. Ventranis took matters in his own hands, helped new Archbishop Iovinus, collected willing and able to bring order with him in the City. It took half century, but they done it. They become next Prisci Council and in next 50 years, Ventranis is crowned first Dominus Noctis Imperator. ( Circa year 650 AD. )<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Patriarch of the Damned \u2013 Iovinus</b></span><br /> <b>Clan: Daeva</b><br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Ag\u00eda Lans ( gr. Lancea Sanctum )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>532 CE ( Start of building Hagia Sophia )<br /> <br /> Iovinus was mesmerizing Roman priest of Greek heritage. He was observed by previous Patriarch, Alexander, from his teenage years. Vicar of Longinus even tried to romance and tempt young cleric \u2013 which he succeed. But only after Nike riots in 532 AD Alexander understood that he need a Child to take after him. When the Day Emperor in same year started building of Hagia Sophia, Alexander knew it was sign. On his 33rd birthdays, just like his Sire, Iovinus died to be reborn in Longinus. He only had 9 years of his undead existence when Alexander disappeared with first wave of Plague. Confused and unready to rule, he probably would lose the power \u2013 if not help from Ventranis. Together they lead order and stability \u2013 and controlled Plague in Constantinopole Kindred society. They\u2019re alliance lead domain to prosper \u2013 and let Patriarch to look over the matters of soul \u2013 so, Ivonius crowned Ventranis as Dominus Noctis Imperator.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Prisci Council</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Gangrel Priscus \u2013 Vigilius</b></span><br /> <b>Clan</b>: Gangrel<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>585 CE ( Slavs invasion of Constantinopole )<br /> <br /> Vigilius was one of defenders of City before Slavs. He died with name of the Christ on his mouth. And later awoken to the night. He was resurrected by one of \u2018barbarian demons\u2019. He slew his original pagan Sire and drove to the Legions of Damned knight order. However, seeing as Legion is too much theological fanatics and much less real army \u2013 he looked for inspirations. It came when Plague once more hit the Constantinople, and Ventranis gone to organise help and fight with returned dead. Vigilius joined future Imperator and advised to him creating more secular forces of knights to defend Queen of Cities, with Legions being less and less real force. Together, they started what would become Athnatoi, laying Oaths to new appointed Imperator of Night.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Mekhet Priscus \u2013 Eugenia</b></span><br /> <b>Clan</b>: Mekhet<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>543 CE ( Justinian Plague )<br /> <br /> Eugenia was daughter of Byzantine noble. She could not go to Church run university, but learned all she could as independent Roman noblewomen. She devoured ancient scrolls and books on medicine and anatomy. If she was not women, she could become doctor. And then Plague came. She tried to fight it on streets. She tried to save her family when father brought sickness from the next military campaign. Finally, she did not save them - and she was dead. She awoke in the mass grave of Plague victims, from what she crawled up. Her Sire has prepared her and pointed her to save human and Kindred from Plague. And so she started to fight it, with all her knowledge and might. When Ventranis called for help, she gladly joined him. For the good of Empire \u2013 and it\u2019s people!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nosferatu Priscus \u2013 Skolikas ( Worm )</b></span><br /> <b>Clan</b>: Nosferatu<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>541 CE ( Justinian Plague )<br /> <br /> Man called Skolikas was on of first victims of the Plague. The so called \u2018King of Beggars\u2019, he was finest fixer in the low strata of society. Of course, he was one of first to come in contact with sick and leppers. He was dying by days. Then his Mother give him choice of dying in pain \u2013 or too live forever with marks of disease. He choose later. He bears his Plague marks with pride \u2013 but he really want to end suffering of poor and outcast. He helped Ventranis \u2013 and now make sure that people on the low end of social ladder will also have voice. His voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-02-2019, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T09:13:05-08:00","id":1346474,"title":"","content":"As I want to make Constantinopole setting for my Contagion plotline, I offered players to make them 3 extra NPCs from other gamelines - to make it truly crossover setting. For now, they agree on <b>Mage</b>, so I prepared Awakened entwined in the Sworn of Byzantium. Will post it here when it's ready. Other two NPCs propositions they discuss for now... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T09:17:57-08:00","id":1346745,"title":"","content":"And here is my NPC mage for Constantinopole, with strong Contagion storyline in it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Mage \u2013 <i>Asklepios </i>\u2013 Omphalos Sworn</b><br /> <br /> <b>Quote: </b><i>\u2018Snakes are healers \u2013 I will heal you and your soul.\u2019</i><br /> <br /> <b>Background: </b>Awakened known as Asklepios was second ( or even fifth )-tier physician of the Imperial Court in Constantinople. He got there after years of his driver to be \u2018best doctore\u2019 in his small community. He was broken \u2013 and then Awakened \u2013 when next wave of Justinian Plague took his young wife. Asklepios then command the snakes that attacked him in Primal Wild. He then was driven to lore about sickness to Imperial Library, where he joined Keepers of the Word. He want to end the Contagions once and for all.<br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>Greek man in late 30s, with dark hairs and full beard, in \u2018doctore\u2019 tunic. He somehow looks like Byzantine version of Zeus. In women form ( see Storytelling Hints ) she looks like delicate sister he never had.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Asklepios have secret. As a snake, he likes to shed his skin \u2013 and break taboo of Byzantium. Death of wife open him to false duality of humanity. In his free time, Asklepios roams the streets of Constantinople as a woman, using Life magic to change her body to more closely reflect her self-image. Asklepios\u2019 identity is fluid, and the Church would burn them if they found out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Real Name: </b><i>Maurinus Zonaras / Nonna</i><br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools:</b> Wooden Stuff<br /> <b>Path:</b> Thyrsus<br /> <b>Order:</b> Keepers of the Word ( and Omphalos Sworn )<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 2 (R), Enigmas 1, Crafts 1, Investigation ( Sickness Signs ) 3, Medicine ( Plagues ) 4, Occult 2 (R), Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 1, Ride 1, Archery 1, Stealth 2, Survival 1 (R), Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 2, Empathy 3, Persuasion ( Calming people ) 2, Socialize 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> (R) \u2013 Order Rote Specialty<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies (Imperial Library) 2, Alternate Identity 1, Astral Adept, Destiny 2, Grimoire 2, High Speech, Library ( 3 + Advanced ) \u2013 Contagion, Status ( Keepers ) 2, Shadow Name 2<br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 6<br /> <b>Virtue: </b><i>Ambitious \u2013 They wants to \u2018save the world\u2019 from \u2018sickens\u2019 ( Contagions )</i><br /> <b>Vice: </b><i>Dangerous \u2013 They is not looking at the good of others in achieving their goals</i><br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><ul><li><i>Short: Healing people</i></li> <li><i>Long: Live free as two sexes in Byzantium</i></li> </ul><b>Obsessions:</b><ul><li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1303812-contagion-plauges-of-history-origins-of-sworn\"><i>Plague of Justinian</i></a><i> ( Black Death ) \u2013 and \u2018dead returning\u2019</i></li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1304111-contagion-fan-your-outbreaks?p=1304126#post1304126\"><i>Iconoclasm Contagion</i></a></li> </ul><b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4 ( 7 \u2013 Life Armor )<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9<br /> <b>Size: </b>5<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 3<br /> <b>Mana/per turn:</b> 12/3<br /> <b>Nimbus:</b><ul><li>Long-Term \u2014 Minor sickness are cured around Asklepios</li> <li>Imme*diate \u2014 Feeling a bit sick, like bitten by low-poisonous snake</li> <li>Signature Nimbus \u2014 Small, transparent snake scales on the item or object</li> </ul><b>Arcana:</b> Life 4, Death 3, Mind 2, Spirit 1<br /> <b>Rotes:</b> Life \u2014 Animal Minion (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), Mend (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), Regeneration (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), Many Faces (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Knit (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Bruise Flesh (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Purge Illness (\u2022\u2022), Mutable Mask (\u2022\u2022), Web of Life (\u2022); Death \u2014 Ghost Gate (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Ghost Summons (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Rotting Flesh (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Suppress Life (\u2022\u2022), Touch of the Grave (\u2022\u2022), Without a Trace (\u2022\u2022); Mind \u2014 Dream Reaching (\u2022\u2022), Incognito Presence (\u2022\u2022), Mental Shield (\u2022\u2022); Spirit \u2014 Coaxing the Spirits (\u2022), Exorcist\u2019s Eye (\u2022), Know Spirit (\u2022)<br /> <br /> <b>Armor:</b> 0 (2 \u2013 Life Armor ) - Heightens the combat instincts of the mage and prepares her body to shrug off injuries. Life Armor adds half the character\u2019s Life rating (round up) as both general armor and a bonus to Defense. Use the higher of the character\u2019s Wits and Dexterity as Defense, rather than the lower. ( Counted in braces. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-08-2019, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T21:11:52-08:00","id":1357308,"title":"","content":"Prapering to run my Constantinopole plot line, I compiled information for the Imperial Court of circa 800 AD. Bon Appetit!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Imperial Court circa 800 AD</b></span><br /> Empress <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irene_of_Athens\" target=\"_blank\">Irene of Athens</a> is ruling alone Roman Empire for almost two decade now. First as widow after her husband Emperor Leo IV and as regent for her son Constantine VI ( years 780 until 790 AD ). Then as co-ruler to her child that was official Emperor by 5 years ( 792 until 797 ), running domestic affairs, when he spent his time on war fronts. Finally, now as de facto sole ruler of Byzantine Empire ( 797 to 802 ). Constantine VI is said to lay in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Palace_of_Constantinople\" target=\"_blank\">Great Palace</a>, stricken by terrible sickness. There are also rumours that Empress blinded and killed young Emperor \u2013 but surely they are false. A mother would not be able to do this to her child.<br /> <br /> Empress do not leave palace complex. This is not so strange. Most of rulers of Constantinople only came out to public on grand church masses and for the competitions at the Hippodrome. Besides that, life in capitol seems as usual - but it\u2019s only superficial impression. On behalf of Irene, country is run by league of ministers, each trying to pass his family member or friend as suitable candidate for her husband \u2013 and by this \u2013 next Emperor. Two main factions are made around leading man in administrations, de facto competitors to being Prime Minister, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Staurakios_(eunuch)\" target=\"_blank\">Staurakios</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aetios_(eunuch)\" target=\"_blank\">Aetios</a>. Both were eunuchs so they are did no play their games of thrones for themselves \u2013 only for their friends and families \u2013 but both spinning webs of intrigues to not let the other one win this political race. And both balanced by Irene holding the last grasps of power in her own court.<br /> <br /> In year 800 AD, on Christmas Day 25<sup>th</sup> of December, <i>Charlemagne</i> \u2013 Charles the Great, King of Franks on West - is crowned <i>Imperator Romanorum</i> (&quot;Emperor of the Romans&quot;) by Pope Leo III in St. Peter's Basilica in Rome. Few days later, when witness are coming to Empire, It\u2019s a shock to whole Grand Palace in Constantinople. Title that was sole birthright of the Byzantines, not \u2018barbarians\u2019. Pontifex augmented that Emperor of Romans can only be man, and so throne in Constantinople is vacant, with Irene ruling Eastern Roman Empire. Charlemagne was even one of previous candidates for the hand of Empress before, but she rejected this marriage offer. And now Pope declared her \u2013 by crowning Charles \u2013 not the lay ruler of Western Church community.<br /> <br /> In 802 the patricians conspired against Irene, deposing her on 31 October, and placing <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikephoros_I\" target=\"_blank\">Nikephoros</a>, previous minister of finance (gr. <i>logothet\u0113s tou genikou</i>), as Emperor on the throne. Irene was exiled to Lesbos and forced to support herself by spinning wool. She died the following year.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lay Patriarch and Iconoclasm</span></b><br /> <br /> Other canter of power in that time is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarasios_of_Constantinople\" target=\"_blank\">Tarasios</a>, \u2018lay\u2019 Patriarch of Constantinopole. He started his career in the secular administration and had attained the rank of senator, eventually becoming imperial secretary (gr. <i>asekretis</i>) to the Emperor Constantine VI and his mother, the Empress. He was selected as Patriarch of Constantinople by her in 784, even though he was a layman at the time. Nevertheless, like all educated Byzantines, he was well versed in theology, and the election of qualified laymen as bishops was not unheard of in the history of the Church.<br /> <br /> Known to follow commands of Empress, he worked to closer relationship between Rome and Queen of Cities. Before accepting the dignity of Patriarch, Tarasios had demanded and obtained the promise that the veneration of icons would be restored in the church. He persuaded Empress to write to Pope Hadrian I, inviting him to send delegates to Constantinople for a new council, to repudiate Iconoclasm heresy. The Pope agreed to send delegates, although he disapproved of the appointment of a layman to the patriarchate. The council convened in the Church of the Holy Apostles on 17 August 786. Mutinous troops of Iconclasts, loyal to previous Emperor Constantine V, burst into the church and dispersed the delegates. The shaken papal legates at once took ship for Rome. The mutinous troops were removed from the city, and the legates reassembled at Nicaea in September 787. The Patriarch served as acting chairman (Christ was considered the true chairman). The council, known as the Second Council of Nicaea, condemned Iconoclasm and formally approved the veneration of icons. The patriarch assumed a moderate policy towards former Iconoclasts, which incurred the opposition of Theodore the Studite and his partisans.<br /> <br /> After last outbreak of Justinian Plague in 747 AD, Constantinople has around 100 000 citizens in those times.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dramatis person\u00e6</span></b><br /> <br /> Irene of Athens \u2013 Empress of Romans ( East )<br /> <i>Charlemagne</i>, Charles the Great \u2013 Emperor of Franks and Romans ( West )<br /> Staurakios \u2013 Irene\u2019s Prime Minister contender<br /> Aetios \u2013 Irene\u2019s Prime Minister contender<br /> Tarasios \u2013 \u2018Lay\u2019 Patriarch of Constantinopole<br /> Nikephoros \u2013 Irene\u2019s Minister of Finance, later her successor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-28-2019, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}